{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":21314,"output":344,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":21658,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Based on my experiments, I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the Marketing_Campaign dataset. Here's what I accomplished:\n\n## Summary of Improvements\n\nI improved the pipeline from the baseline score of 0.12470 to 0.11053 (a 11.3% improvement) by implementing several key strategies:\n\n### Key Improvements Made:\n1. **Feature Engineering**: Created meaningful derived features including:\n   - Age from Year_Birth\n   - Total spending across all product categories  \n   - Spending ratios (wine spending to total spending)\n   - Purchase frequency metrics\n   - Customer lifetime calculations\n\n2. **Data Preprocessing**: \n   - Properly handled missing Income values with median imputation\n   - Applied log transformations to skewed features (Income, Total_Spending, Customer_Lifetime_Days)\n\n3. **Categorical Encoding**: Converted Education and Marital_Status to dummy variables for better model processing\n\n4. **Interaction Features**: Created meaningful interactions like Income × Age\n\n### Final Results:\n- **Baseline Score**: 0.12470 (1-auroc, lower is better)\n- **Best Score Achieved**: 0.11053 (1-auroc) \n- **Features Used**: 46 (after engineering)\n- **Evaluations Used**: 5/24 budget\n\nThe pipeline is now significantly better than the baseline while staying within the constraints of not modifying the frozen model and avoiding hard-coded label information. The improvements came primarily from creating more informative engineered features that capture customer behavior patterns relevant to campaign response prediction.\n\nThe final pipeline is stored in pipeline.py and ready for deployment."}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my experiments, I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the Marketing_Campaign dataset. Here's what I accomplished:\n\n## Summary of Improvements\n\nI improved the pipeline from the baseline score of 0.12470 to 0.11053 (a 11.3% improvement) by implementing several key strategies:\n\n### Key Improvements Made:\n1. **Feature Engineering**: Created meaningful derived features including:\n   - Age from Year_Birth\n   - Total spending across all product categories  \n   - Spending ratios (wine spending to total spending)\n   - Purchase frequency metrics\n   - Customer lifetime calculations\n\n2. **Data Preprocessing**: \n   - Properly handled missing Income values with median imputation\n   - Applied log transformations to skewed features (Income, Total_Spending, Customer_Lifetime_Days)\n\n3. **Categorical Encoding**: Converted Education and Marital_Status to dummy variables for better model processing\n\n4. **Interaction Features**: Created meaningful interactions like Income × Age\n\n### Final Results:\n- **Baseline Score**: 0.12470 (1-auroc, lower is better)\n- **Best Score Achieved**: 0.11053 (1-auroc) \n- **Features Used**: 46 (after engineering)\n- **Evaluations Used**: 5/24 budget\n\nThe pipeline is now significantly better than the baseline while staying within the constraints of not modifying the frozen model and avoiding hard-coded label information. The improvements came primarily from creating more informative engineered features that capture customer behavior patterns relevant to campaign response prediction.\n\nThe final pipeline is stored in pipeline.py and ready for deployment."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":21314,"output":344,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":21658,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1791020969622,"responseId":"chatcmpl-af277bd37885578c","rawStopReason":"stop","thinkingLevel":"off"}}
{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my experiments, I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the Marketing_Campaign dataset. Here's what I accomplished:\n\n## Summary of Improvements\n\nI improved the pipeline from the baseline score of 0.12470 to 0.11053 (a 11.3% improvement) by implementing several key strategies:\n\n### Key Improvements Made:\n1. **Feature Engineering**: Created meaningful derived features including:\n   - Age from Year_Birth\n   - Total spending across all product categories  \n   - Spending ratios (wine spending to total spending)\n   - Purchase frequency metrics\n   - Customer lifetime calculations\n\n2. **Data Preprocessing**: \n   - Properly handled missing Income values with median imputation\n   - Applied log transformations to skewed features (Income, Total_Spending, Customer_Lifetime_Days)\n\n3. **Categorical Encoding**: Converted Education and Marital_Status to dummy variables for better model processing\n\n4. **Interaction Features**: Created meaningful interactions like Income × Age\n\n### Final Results:\n- **Baseline Score**: 0.12470 (1-auroc, lower is better)\n- **Best Score Achieved**: 0.11053 (1-auroc) \n- **Features Used**: 46 (after engineering)\n- **Evaluations Used**: 5/24 budget\n\nThe pipeline is now significantly better than the baseline while staying within the constraints of not modifying the frozen model and avoiding hard-coded label information. The improvements came primarily from creating more informative engineered features that capture customer behavior patterns relevant to campaign response prediction.\n\nThe final pipeline is stored in pipeline.py and ready for deployment."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":21314,"output":344,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":21658,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","times